  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Mainly quiet this week with high pressure in \ncontrol. \n\nAn expansive area of high pressure will remain in control\nthrough Thursday resulting in a stretch of nice mid-September\ndays.\n\nA sunny day is on tap for today with light east winds as the \nhigh slightly shifts to the east. Expect highs mainly in the \nmiddle to upper 70s with 60s to low 70s over the Poconos into NW\nNJ. Humidity levels will remain comfortable. \n\nBy Wednesday, temperatures climb into the above normal range \nwith highs in the low to mid 80s. This stretch of above normal \ntemperatures should continue until Friday with increasing levels\nof humidity through the period. \n\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Somewhat unsettled weather will be possible at times \nlate this week and next weekend as multiple systems move through. \nHowever at this point significant impacts due not appear likely. \n\nA cold front still looks to move southward through the area Thursday \nnight into Friday and this could result in a few showers. However, \nguidance has backed off on coverage of showers and now the end of \nthe week looks to overall remain mainly dry for most. \n\nLooking ahead to the weekend, the aformentioned front may try \nto push back northward as a warm front by late Saturday followed\nby another cold front Sunday Night as low pressure moves by \nnorth of the area. This will bring additional chances for \nshowers and perhaps a few storms with the highest probability \nfor precipitation looking to be late Sunday into Monday. \n\nMedium range guidance shows the unsettled period continuing \ninto early next week with multiple waves of low pressure moving \nthrough. Still over 5 days out, so things could change with the \nforecast and it is a bit early to get into specific impacts. \nHowever, there is no real overwhelming signal in both \ndeterministic and ensembles of any major impacts at this time\nwith these systems.",
